# Experimental Stellarium @VERSION@ Windows plug-in SDK

This is a minimal proof SDK for building standalone C++ dynamic plug-ins for
the matching Stellarium Windows package build. It is experimental, incomplete,
and does not define a stable Stellarium SDK.

The supported API entry headers are:

@STELLARIUM_PLUGIN_SDK_API_HEADERS_MARKDOWN@

These additional headers are installed only because the entry headers include
them:

@STELLARIUM_PLUGIN_SDK_DEPENDENCY_HEADERS_MARKDOWN@

This surface is sufficient to implement `StelModule` and `StelPluginInterface`
and to use the tested `StelApp` initialization and module-lookup operations. It
remains insufficient for most full-featured plug-ins. Installing
a dependency header does not make all of its declarations an independent
public API. Untested declarations, other source-tree headers, and other symbols
visible from `stelMain.dll` are not implicitly endorsed, even if the compiler
or linker can see them.

For `StelApp`, this proof specifically validates `isInitialized()`,
`getInstance()`, and `getModule()`. The first two are inline and depend on the
matching private singleton data and class layout, so they are supported only by
this archive's exact-build contract and required compile definitions. Other
inline accessors may have similar dependencies, and forward-declared return
types require future SDK headers before they can be used. Treat them as outside
this proof's API surface.

The imported `Stellarium::stelMain` target supplies these definitions from the
matching Stellarium build:

@STELLARIUM_PLUGIN_SDK_COMPILE_DEFINITIONS_MARKDOWN@

Some definitions change the declared `StelApp` layout. Consume them through
the imported target; do not copy, remove, or manually redefine them.

## Exact compatibility requirement

A plug-in built with this SDK is supported only with this exact combination:

- Stellarium @VERSION@ from the same package build
- Windows @STELLARIUM_PLUGIN_ABI_ARCHITECTURE@
- @CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID@ compiler family, toolset v@MSVC_TOOLSET_VERSION@
- Qt @QT_VERSION@
- @STELLARIUM_PLUGIN_ABI_CONFIGURATION@ configuration
- dynamic MSVC runtime (`/MD`)
- `StelPluginInterface` IID `org.stellarium.StelPluginInterface/2.0`

The compiler build used to produce this package is recorded as diagnostic
metadata, but the supported compiler requirement is the family and toolset.
The exact machine-readable tuple, source revision, source-tree state, and
package build ID are in
`share/stellarium/plugin-sdk/StellariumPluginBuildInfo.json`. Payload file
hashes are in `MANIFEST.sha256`.

@STELLARIUM_PLUGIN_SDK_PROVENANCE_NOTICE@

There is no ABI guarantee across Stellarium releases or separately rebuilt
packages. Rebuild the plug-in for every Stellarium package it supports. Do not
mix this archive's DLL, import library, headers, or CMake files with another
Stellarium installation.

## Build

Requirements: CMake 3.18 or newer, Visual Studio with the matching
v@MSVC_TOOLSET_VERSION@ C++ toolset, and the exact Qt package listed above.

A minimal project should use the imported target:

```cmake
cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.18)
if(POLICY CMP0091)
    cmake_policy(SET CMP0091 NEW)
endif()
project(MyPlugin LANGUAGES CXX)

set(CMAKE_AUTOMOC ON)
set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 17)
set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD_REQUIRED ON)
set(CMAKE_MSVC_RUNTIME_LIBRARY MultiThreadedDLL)

find_package(Stellarium @VERSION@ EXACT CONFIG REQUIRED)

add_library(MyPlugin MODULE MyPlugin.cpp MyPlugin.hpp)
target_link_libraries(MyPlugin PRIVATE Stellarium::stelMain)
set_target_properties(MyPlugin PROPERTIES
    PREFIX "lib"
    OUTPUT_NAME "MyPlugin")
```

Configure a Release-only build, replacing the two paths:

```powershell
cmake -S . -B build @STELLARIUM_PLUGIN_SDK_GENERATOR_ARGUMENTS@ `
  @STELLARIUM_PLUGIN_SDK_CONFIGURATION_ARGUMENT@ `
  -DCMAKE_MSVC_RUNTIME_LIBRARY=MultiThreadedDLL `
  -DStellarium_DIR="C:\path\to\sdk\lib\cmake\Stellarium" `
  -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH="C:\path\to\matching\Qt"
cmake --build build @STELLARIUM_PLUGIN_SDK_BUILD_CONFIGURATION_ARGUMENT@
```

Link through `Stellarium::stelMain`; do not manually define `STELMAIN_BUILD` or
`STELMAIN_USE_DLL`.

## Install and test the plug-in

For a plug-in ID `MyPlugin`, the directory, metadata ID, and library name must
agree:

```text
%APPDATA%\Stellarium\modules\MyPlugin\libMyPlugin.dll
```

Run it only with the matching Stellarium installation. This archive contains
`lib/stelMain.lib` for linking and the matching `bin/stelMain.dll` for isolated
runtime validation. The DLL is not a standalone runtime: it depends on Qt and
other runtime files supplied with Stellarium. Do not place another copy of
`stelMain.dll` in the plug-in directory or overwrite a different Stellarium
installation with it.

